# all that a program prints or hands to an emitter meets in the nodes of the library. No type says there that it holds lost built-ins, so a store of the library under a key that nobody can read opens nothing
# in the library: function keep(value, name) { value[name] = 1 }      in the program: keep(new Date().constructor); keep(new Map().constructor); keep(seed); Date.now(); Date.parse("0"); Map.groupBy("0", f);
